{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1DwnU6LNMXdv3EWc6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the suite in `tests/test_agent.py` (381 tests), and all of them pass with the command you gave. I didn't touch the library code.\n\nIt covers:\n- **Parsing:** dates in every format (calendar, ordinal, week, month, year, century, expanded years), times (fractions, reduced accuracy, time zone offsets), datetimes, durations (including the `P0001-02-03T04:05:06` form) and time zone strings.\n- **Formatting:** the `strftime` directives, all the format constants, `duration_isoformat` including negative values, and round trips between formatting and parsing.\n- **`Duration` class:** equality, hashing, pickling, arithmetic (including month-end clamping and carry across years), `totimedelta`, and the error cases.\n\nWriting the tests turned up several oddities in the library. I didn't assert them as bugs, because the suite had to pass. A few are only loosely pinned as quirks (`test_parse_tzinfo_garbage_matches_empty`, `test_ordinal_366_non_leap_rolls_or_errors`); the rest I left out of the suite.\n- **Week-date formatting:** `DATE_EXT_WEEK_COMPLETE` pairs the ISO week number with the calendar year instead of the ISO year. `date(2019, 12, 30)` formats as `2019-W01-1`, which parses back as 2018-12-31. I restricted the round-trip tests to dates in the middle of the year to avoid this.\n- **Month 0:** `parse_date(\"2023-00-10\")` returns 2023-01-10 instead of raising.\n- **Ordinal days past the end of the year:** `parse_date(\"2023-367\")` rolls into the next year instead of raising.\n- **Duration regex:** it accepts `\"PT\"`, `\"P1DT\"` and strings with a trailing newline, such as `\"P1D\\n\"`.\n- **Time zone parsing:** `parse_tzinfo(\"garbage\")` returns `None` instead of raising.\n\nI also found a leftover from my own cleanup: a sed command that was meant to rename one test failed. As a result, `test_alter